{
  "raw": {
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/uccrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=094961": {
      "title": "Lecturer (Below the Bar) in Medical Imaging and Radiation Therapy (0.5 FTE), School of Medicine",
      "description": "Closing Date: 27/10/2026 Lecturer (Below the Bar) in Medical Imaging and Radiation Therapy (0.5 FTE), School of Medicine Fixed Term Part-Time (0.5FTE) Post (duration November 2027) UCC wishes to appoint an academic to the role of Lecturer in Medical Imaging and Radiation Therapy (0.5FTE). Reporting to the Head of Department, the successful candidate will play a key role in teaching, research and leadership. The successful candidate will support the delivery of the 2-year MSc in Diagnostic Radiography and the MSc in Medical Imaging and Radiation Science online. The successful candidate will hold a BSc or MSc in Diagnostic Radiography or a related discipline, and ideally possess a PhD or equivalent. Duties will include research-led classroom and on-line teaching, examining, development of new course offerings. We expect to recruit hardworking people committed to excellence in teaching, curriculum development, and research dissemination. The role is in-person, primarily based in University College Cork, Brookfield Health Sciences Complex, Cork. Please note that Garda vetting and/or an international police clearance check may form part of the selection process. For an information package including full details of the post, selection criteria and application process see https://ore.ucc.ie/. The University, at its discretion, may undertake to make an additional appointment(s) from this competition following the conclusion of the process. Informal enquiries can be made in confidence to Professor Mark McEntee, email: mark.mcentee@ucc.ie For further information on the Department: https://www.ucc.ie/en/medical/medicalimagingradiationtherapy/ University College Cork is committed to being a fully inclusive global university which actively recruits, supports and retains colleagues from all sectors of society. Equality, Diversity and Inclusion (EDI) are core values under our UCC Strategic Plan 2023-2028. UCC holds a Silver Athena SWAN award in recognition of our commitment to advancing equality in higher education. We value diversity as well as celebrate, support and thrive on the contributions of all our employees and the communities they represent. We are proud to be an equal opportunities employer and encourage applications from everybody, regardless of age, care-giving status, disability, ethnicity, gender and/or gender identity or expression status, nationality, marital status/civil partnership, pregnancy and maternity, race, religion/creed, and/or sexual orientation. We are committed to supporting all staff through flexible working schemes, family-friendly policies, training and development, and staff networks. We value the enrichment that comes from a diverse community and seek to promote equality, prevent discrimination and protect the human rights of each individual in line with equality legislation. We encourage applicants to consult our Dignity and Respect Policy and learn more about our EDI related initiatives . Appointment may be made on the Lecturer (Below the Bar) Salary Scale: €43,028 - €73,909 (Scale B) / €45,116 - €70,327 (Scale A) (pro-rata). Salary placement on appointment will be in accordance with public sector pay policy. We encourage you to reach out to us directly should you require assistance or reasonable accommodation during the recruitment process. Please note interviews will be conducted either online via Microsoft Teams or in person in the first instance. Candidates may also be required to attend interviews in person if an interview takes place online. Candidates will be notified as appropriate **.** Applications must be submitted online via the University College Cork vacancy portal ( https://ore.ucc.ie/ ). Queries relating to the online application process should be referred to recruitment@ucc.ie, quoting the job-title. Candidates should apply, in confidence, before 12 noon (Irish Local Time) on Tuesday, 27th October 2026 No late applications will be accepted. UNIVERSITY COLLEGE CORK IS AN EQUAL OPPORTUNITIES EMPLOYER ** Please note that an appointment to posts advertised will be dependent on University approval, together with the terms of the employment control framework for the higher education sector ** Contact Person : Professor Mark McEntee Contact Email : mark.mcentee@ucc.ie Job ID : 094961 Contact Number : Close Date : 27-Oct-2026 12:00 "
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/uccrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=099215": {
      "title": "Adjunct Appointments & Adjunct Clinical Appointments (New), College of Medicine & Health",
      "description": "Closing Date: 03/11/2026 Adjunct Appointments & Adjunct Clinical Appointments (New), College of Medicine & Health The Head of College, Prof Helen Whelton, is pleased to open the application process for Adjunct Positions within the College of Medicine and Health. Please download and read the attached Candidate Instruction Path in full before starting your application. Important Information • The call is open from Friday 4th September 2026 until 12 noon on Tuesday 3rd November 2026. • Only fully completed applications submitted via the UCC HR portal will be reviewed by the College of Medicine and Health Adjunct Appointments Committee. • Successful applicants will receive one of the honorary titles listed below: - Adjunct Professor - Adjunct Senior Lecturer - Adjunct Lecturer - Adjunct Clinical Professor - Adjunct Clinical Senior Lecturer - Adjunct Clinical Lecturer • Appointments are for 3 years and are subject to renewal following review of application by the Adjunct Appointments Committee. Please refer to the Regulation for Adjunct Appointments for full details. Who should NOT use this route of application Specialist Registrar / Registrar Non-Consulting Hospital Doctors working in clinical sites affiliated to UCC School of Medicine should not apply for adjunct appointment through this College level call. - A separate call will be made by the School of Medicine in July 2027 for the specific 1-year Adjunct Clinical Lectureship. Consultants with School of Medicine Clinical Senior Lecturer (CSL) contracts. - Medical Consultants are eligible to hold a CSL contract with the School of Medicine. - Go to UCC Job Vacancies for School of Medicine CSL applications (rolling call). There will be a separate University level call for promotion for previously appointed School of Medicine CSLs to Clinical Professor (date to be confirmed by UCC People and Culture). If you have any queries, please contact the relevant Head of School as outlined below: Medicine - Dean of School of Medicine - dsom@ucc.ie Dental School - Prof. Paul Brady - paul.brady@ucc.ie Nursing & Midwifery - Prof. Patricia Leahy-Warren - patricia.leahy@ucc.ie Pharmacy - Prof. Abina Crean - a.crean@ucc.ie Public Health - Prof. Ella Arensman - ella.arensman@ucc.ie Clinical Therapies - Prof. Joseph McVeigh - joseph.mcveigh@ucc.ie Contact Person : Relevant Head of School as outlined in advert Contact Email : Job ID : 099215 Contact Number : Close Date : 03-Nov-2026 12:00 "
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/uccrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=099214": {
      "title": "Adjunct Appointments & Adjunct Clinical Appointments (Renewal), College of Medicine & Health",
      "description": "Closing Date: 03/11/2026 Adjunct Appointments & Adjunct Clinical Appointments (Renewal), College of Medicine & Health The Head of College, Prof Helen Whelton, is pleased to open the application process for Renewal of Adjunct Positions within the College of Medicine and Health. Please download and review the attached Candidate Instruction path. Candidates seeking to renew their adjunct appointment at the same level should first consult with relevant Head of Academic Department/ Head of School/ Head of Research functional area before submitting their application. If the case for the appointment is considered sustainable by the School, the completed and signed application form should be submitted for the consideration and approval of the College of Medicine and Health Adjunct Appointments Committee. Important information • The call is open from Friday 4th September 2026 until 12 noon on Tuesday 3rd November 2026. • Only fully completed applications submitted via the UCC HR portal will be reviewed by the College of Medicine and Health Adjunct Appointments Committee. • The successful re-appointment of an individual with one of the titles below is an honorary appointment with an honorary title: - Adjunct Professor - Adjunct Senior Lecturer - Adjunct Lecturer - Adjunct Clinical Professor - Adjunct Clinical Senior Lecturer - Adjunct Clinical Lecturer • Renewed appointments are for 3 years and are subject to further renewal following review of application by the Adjunct Appointments Committee. Please refer to the Regulation for Adjunct Appointments for full details. If it is decided by the applicant and Head of School to change the level of appointment, please follow the process for Application for Adjunct positions here: Adjunct Appointments & Adjunct Clinical Appointments (New) If you have any queries, please contact the relevant Head of School as outlined below: Medicine - Dean of School of Medicine - dsom@ucc.ie Dental School - Prof. Paul Brady - paul.brady@ucc.ie Nursing & Midwifery - Prof. Patricia Leahy-Warren - patricia.leahy@ucc.ie Pharmacy - Prof. Abina Crean - a.crean@ucc.ie Public Health - Prof. Ella Arensman - ella.arensman@ucc.ie Clinical Therapies - Prof. Joseph McVeigh - joseph.mcveigh@ucc.ie Contact Person : Relevant Head of School as outlined in advert Contact Email : Job ID : 099214 Contact Number : Close Date : 03-Nov-2026 12:00 "
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/uccrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=097762": {
      "title": "Clinical Skills Simulation Resource Centre Manager, School of Nursing and Midwifery, College of Medicine and Health",
      "description": "Closing Date: 03/11/2026 Clinical Skills Simulation Resource Centre Manager, School of Nursing and Midwifery, College of Medicine and Health Specific Purpose Whole Time Post (anticipated duration March 2028) UCC wishes to appoint a Clinical Skills Simulation Resource Centre (CSSRC) Manager, in the School of Nursing and Midwifery. Reporting to the Head of School, the successful candidate will lead and manage the CSSRC, working closely with the existing CSSRC team, academic team, professional support staff and clinical partners. The appointable candidate will deliver strategic management, supporting the implementation of simulation-based learning, teaching and assessment and related activities across undergraduate and postgraduate nursing and midwifery programmes. The CSSRC has significant simulation-based capabilities including low-fidelity task trainers, anatomical models, high-fidelity patient simulators, standardised participants and is developing virtual/immersive/online simulation approaches. The successful candidate will provide strategic leadership and play a core role in resource planning and the ongoing development of the CSSRC. Please note that Garda vetting and/or an international police clearance check may form part of the selection process. For an information package including full details of the post, selection criteria and application process see https://ore.ucc.ie/. The University, at its discretion, may undertake to make an additional appointment(s) from this competition following the conclusion of the process. Informal enquiries can be made in confidence to Ms. Regina Murphy, School Manager, School of Nursing and Midwifery, UCC, Tel: +353-21-4901550, Email: regina.murphy@ucc.ie For further information on the school please see Nursing and Midwifery | University College Cork University College Cork is committed to being a fully inclusive global university which actively recruits, supports and retains colleagues from all sectors of society. Equality, Diversity and Inclusion (EDI) are core values under our UCC Strategic Plan 2023-2028. UCC holds a Silver Athena SWAN award in recognition of our commitment to advancing equality in higher education. We value diversity as well as celebrate, support and thrive on the contributions of all our employees and the communities they represent. We are proud to be an equal opportunities employer and encourage applications from everybody, regardless of age, care-giving status, disability, ethnicity, gender and/or gender identity or expression status, nationality, marital status/civil partnership, pregnancy and maternity, race, religion/creed, and/or sexual orientation. We are committed to supporting all staff through flexible working schemes, family-friendly policies, training and development, and staff networks. We value the enrichment that comes from a diverse community and seek to promote equality, prevent discrimination and protect the human rights of each individual in line with equality legislation. We encourage applicants to consult our Dignity and Respect Policy and learn more about our EDI related initiatives . Appointment may be made on the HSE Clinical Nurse Manager III Salary Scale: €71,432 - €80,671 (Scale B). Salary placement on appointment will be in accordance with public sector pay policy. We encourage you to reach out to us directly should you require assistance or reasonable accommodation during the recruitment process. Please note interviews will be conducted either online via Microsoft Teams or in person in the first instance. Candidates may also be required to attend interviews in person if an interview takes place online. Candidates will be notified as appropriate . Applications must be submitted online via the University College Cork vacancy portal (https://ore.ucc.ie/). Queries relating to the online application process should be referred to recruitment@ucc.ie, quoting the job-title. Candidates should apply, in confidence, before 12 noon (Irish Local Time) on Tuesday, 3rd November 2026 No late applications will be accepted. UNIVERSITY COLLEGE CORK IS AN EQUAL OPPORTUNITIES EMPLOYER Please note that an appointment to posts advertised will be dependent on University approval, together with the terms of the employment control framework for the higher education sector Contact Person : Regina Murphy Contact Email : regina.murphy@ucc.ie Job ID : 097762 Contact Number : Close Date : 03-Nov-2026 12:00 "
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/uccrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=096636": {
      "title": "Lecturer (Above the Bar) In Mathematics, School of Mathematical Sciences, College of Science, Engineering and Food Science",
      "description": "Closing Date: 20/10/2026 Lecturer (Above the Bar) In Mathematics, School of Mathematical Sciences, College of Science, Engineering and Food Science Permanent Whole Time Post UCC wishes to appoint an academic to the role of Lecturer (Above the Bar) in Mathematics. Applicants from all areas of Mathematics are invited to apply. Reporting to the Head of School, the appointee will play a pivotal role in the development of Mathematics in the School and across the University. The successful candidate will help develop the research profile of Mathematics, working collaboratively with colleagues. These are key academic roles with responsibility for leading or contributing to the School’s delivery of BSc and MSc programmes, driving growth in PhD enrolment, and embedding mathematical research across the Research Clusters within University College Cork’s Futures Research Initiative. The School has an established international partner and the successful candidate will be expected to foster this relationship through practical commitment to internationalization in teaching and research activities. Please note that Garda vetting and/or an international police clearance check may form part of the selection process. For an information package including full details of the post, selection criteria and application process see https://ore.ucc.ie/. The University, at its discretion, may undertake to make an additional appointment(s) from this competition following the conclusion of the process. Informal enquiries can be made in confidence to Dr Martin Kilian, Head of School via email to M.Kilian@ucc.ie or to Professor Robert Osburn, Head of the Mathematics Discipline, via email to robert.osburn@ucc.ie For further information on the school can be found on our website, Mathematical Sciences | University College Cork . University College Cork is committed to being a fully inclusive global university which actively recruits, supports and retains colleagues from all sectors of society. Equality, Diversity and Inclusion (EDI) are core values under our UCC Strategic Plan 2023-2028. UCC holds a Silver Athena SWAN award in recognition of our commitment to advancing equality in higher education. We value diversity as well as celebrate, support and thrive on the contributions of all our employees and the communities they represent. We are proud to be an equal opportunities employer and encourage applications from everybody, regardless of age, care-giving status, disability, ethnicity, gender and/or gender identity or expression status, nationality, marital status/civil partnership, pregnancy and maternity, race, religion/creed, and/or sexual orientation. We are committed to supporting all staff through flexible working schemes, family-friendly policies, training and development, and staff networks. We value the enrichment that comes from a diverse community and seek to promote equality, prevent discrimination and protect the human rights of each individual in line with equality legislation. We encourage applicants to consult our Dignity and Respect Policy and learn more about our EDI related initiatives . Appointment may be made on the Lecturer (Above the Bar) Salary Scale: €80,776 - €104,610 (Scale B) / €76,852 - €99,378 (Scale A). Salary placement on appointment will be in accordance with public sector pay policy. We encourage you to reach out to us directly should you require assistance or reasonable accommodation during the recruitment process. Please note interviews will be conducted either online via Microsoft Teams or in person in the first instance. Candidates may also be required to attend interviews in person if an interview takes place online. Candidates will be notified as appropriate . Applications must be submitted online via the University College Cork vacancy portal (https://ore.ucc.ie/). Queries relating to the online application process should be referred to recruitment@ucc.ie, quoting the job-title. Candidates should apply, in confidence, before 12 noon (Irish Local Time) on Tuesday, 20th October 2026. No late applications will be accepted. UNIVERSITY COLLEGE CORK IS AN EQUAL OPPORTUNITIES EMPLOYER Please note that an appointment to posts advertised will be dependent on University approval, together with the terms of the employment control framework for the higher education sector Contact Person : Dr Martin Kilian Contact Email : M.Kilian@ucc.ie Job ID : 096636 Contact Number : Close Date : 20-Oct-2026 12:00 "
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/uccrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=099373": {
      "title": "Lecturer (Above the Bar) In Public Health Nursing, School of Nursing and Midwifery, College of Medicine and Health",
      "description": "Closing Date: 27/10/2026 Lecturer (Above the Bar) In Public Health Nursing, School of Nursing and Midwifery, College of Medicine and Health Permanent- Whole Time Post UCC wishes to appoint to the role of Lecturer (Above the Bar) in Public Health Nursing. The appointee will be expected to contribute to teaching, assessment, scholarly activity and programme development and administration at undergraduate and postgraduate level, as well as engage in relevant research. The successful appointee will hold a professional nursing qualification, have held or hold a registration (or be eligible to register) in Public Health Nursing with the Nursing and Midwifery Board of Ireland. Applicants will be expected to have an academic qualification to Master’s level and be registered for or have completed a PhD / Doctorate. Applicants are also expected to have considerable public health nursing/ community health nursing experience. The School of Nursing and Midwifery was established in 1994 and since then a wide range of programmes have been developed at both undergraduate, postgraduate and doctorate levels. In addition, the School has a growing suite of Continuing Professional Development modules supporting life-long learning. Since 2012, the School has actively engaged in international recruitment and now has a growing body of international students. The School now has over 1,400 students and is one of the largest in the University. The School is committed to excellence and leadership in teaching, practice and research involving close collaborative relationships with health service providers, and national and international educators and researchers. The School holds the Athena Swan Bronze Award and is in the top 30 in QS subject Rankings for Nursing. Please note that Garda vetting and/or an international police clearance check may form part of the selection process. For an information package including full details of the post, selection criteria and application process see https://ore.ucc.ie/. The University, at its discretion, may undertake to make an additional appointment(s) from this competition following the conclusion of the process. Informal enquiries can be made in confidence to Professor Patricia Leahy-Warren, Tel: 021-4901462/1553, Email: headofsonm@ucc.ie For further information on the school please see Nursing and Midwifery | University College Cork University College Cork is committed to being a fully inclusive global university which actively recruits, supports and retains colleagues from all sectors of society. Equality, Diversity and Inclusion (EDI) are core values under our UCC Strategic Plan 2023-2028. UCC holds a Silver Athena SWAN award in recognition of our commitment to advancing equality in higher education. We value diversity as well as celebrate, support and thrive on the contributions of all our employees and the communities they represent. We are proud to be an equal opportunities employer and encourage applications from everybody, regardless of age, care-giving status, disability, ethnicity, gender and/or gender identity or expression status, nationality, marital status/civil partnership, pregnancy and maternity, race, religion/creed, and/or sexual orientation. We are committed to supporting all staff through flexible working schemes, family-friendly policies, training and development, and staff networks. We value the enrichment that comes from a diverse community and seek to promote equality, prevent discrimination and protect the human rights of each individual in line with equality legislation. We encourage applicants to consult our Dignity and Respect Policy and learn more about our EDI related initiatives . Appointment may be made on Lecturer (Above Bar) Salary Scale: €80,776 - €104,610 (Scale B) / €76,852 - €99,378 (Scale A). Salary placement on appointment will be in accordance with public sector pay policy. We encourage you to reach out to us directly should you require assistance or reasonable accommodation during the recruitment process. Please note interviews will be conducted either online via Microsoft Teams or in person in the first instance. Candidates may also be required to attend interviews in person if an interview takes place online. Candidates will be notified as appropriate. Applications must be submitted online via the University College Cork vacancy portal (https://ore.ucc.ie/). Queries relating to the online application process should be referred to recruitment@ucc.ie, quoting the job-title. Candidates should apply, in confidence, before 12 noon (Irish Local Time) on Tuesday, 27th October 2026 No late applications will be accepted. UNIVERSITY COLLEGE CORK IS AN EQUAL OPPORTUNITIES EMPLOYER Please note that an appointment to posts advertised will be dependent on University approval, together with the terms of the employment control framework for the higher education sector Contact Person : Professor Patricia Leahy-Warren Contact Email : headofsonm@ucc.ie Job ID : 099373 Contact Number : 021-4901462 Close Date : 27-Oct-2026 12:00 "
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/uccrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=098377": {
      "title": "Lecturer (Below the Bar) in Strategy and International Business, Cork University Business School",
      "description": "Closing Date: 10/11/2026 Lecturer (Below the Bar) in Strategy and International Business, Cork University Business School Permanent Whole-Time Post Cork University Business School (CUBS), University College Cork (UCC) wishes to appoint an academic to the role of Lecturer (Below the Bar) in Strategy and International Business. Reporting to the Head of Department , we are inviting applications from those with a background in Strategy & International Business, broadly defined, who are committed to a programme of intellectually rigorous and relevant scholarship that is publishable in top journals and creating wider impact, while also being interested and capable of delivering high-quality, engaged teaching across undergraduate and postgraduate levels. Applicants should demonstrate a track record of relevant research and teaching experience. You should identify your research outputs to date and demonstrate your ongoing potential to publish in leading international journals (3 and 4 star ranked journals by the Chartered Association of Business Schools are preferred), and how you may fit the Centre for the Future of Work and the Economy and/or the various UCC Futures. CUBS holds Triple Accreditation from AACSB, AMBA and EQUIS and since 2024 has held an Athena Swan Bronze Award in recognition of its commitment to advancing gender equality. UCC is ranked in the top 250 universities in the world in the QS Rankings and is proud to be ranked in the world’s top 10 for sustainability. Cork University Business School seeks to shape leaders for a sustainable future with implementation of our strategic vision - Making a difference: Vision to Impact 2026-30 -driving what we do. We are a school that believes that the pursuit of profitability and productivity must be better balanced with the health and wellness of the individual, and the wider environmental and social impact of business decisions. We are committed to providing a dynamic, supportive and inclusive learning, teaching, research and working environment, which recognises the diverse backgrounds and interests of both students and staff. If you want to contribute to delivering our mission and advancing our strategic objectives then this post may be for you. Please note that Garda vetting and/or an international police clearance check may form part of the selection process. For an information package including full details of the post, selection criteria and application process see https://ore.ucc.ie/. The University, at its discretion, may undertake to make an additional appointment(s) from this competition following the conclusion of the process. Informal enquiries can be made in confidence to Professor Lawrence Dooley Email: l.dooley@ucc.ie or Professor Mary McCarthy Email: m.mccarthy@ucc.ie. For further information on the Department https://www.cubsucc.com/ University College Cork is committed to being a fully inclusive global university which actively recruits, supports and retains colleagues from all sectors of society. Equality, Diversity and Inclusion (EDI) are core values under our UCC Strategic Plan 2023-2028. UCC holds a Silver Athena SWAN award in recognition of our commitment to advancing equality in higher education. We value diversity as well as celebrate, support and thrive on the contributions of all our employees and the communities they represent. We are proud to be an equal opportunities employer and encourage applications from everybody, regardless of age, care-giving status, disability, ethnicity, gender and/or gender identity or expression status, nationality, marital status/civil partnership, pregnancy and maternity, race, religion/creed, and/or sexual orientation. We are committed to supporting all staff through flexible working schemes, family-friendly policies, training and development, and staff networks. We value the enrichment that comes from a diverse community and seek to promote equality, prevent discrimination and protect the human rights of each individual in line with equality legislation. We encourage applicants to consult our Dignity and Respect Policy and learn more about our EDI related initiatives . Appointment may be made on the Lecturer Below the Bar Salary Scale: €43,028 - €73,909 (Scale B) / €45,116 - €70,327 (Scale A). Salary placement on appointment will be in accordance with public sector pay policy. We encourage you to reach out to us directly should you require assistance or reasonable accommodation during the recruitment process. Please note interviews will be conducted either online via Microsoft Teams or in person in the first instance. Candidates may also be required to attend interviews in person if an interview takes place online. Candidates will be notified as appropriate. Applications must be submitted online via the University College Cork vacancy portal (https://ore.ucc.ie/). Queries relating to the online application process should be referred to recruitment@ucc.ie, quoting the job-title. Please note that the anticipated start date for this post is August 2027. Candidates should apply, in confidence, before 12 noon (Irish Local Time) on Tuesday, 10th November 2026 No late applications will be accepted. UNIVERSITY COLLEGE CORK IS AN EQUAL OPPORTUNITIES EMPLOYER Please note that an appointment to posts advertised will be dependent on University approval, together with the terms of the employment control framework for the higher education sector Contact Person : Professor Lawrence Dooley Contact Email : l.dooley@ucc.ie Job ID : 098377 Contact Number : Close Date : 10-Nov-2026 12:00 "
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/uccrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=099473": {
      "title": "Post-Doctoral Researcher / Senior Post-Doctoral Researcher - School of Biological, Earth, and Environmental Sciences",
      "description": "Closing Date: 23/10/2026 Post-Doctoral Researcher / Senior Post-Doctoral Researcher - School of Biological, Earth, and Environmental Sciences 30 Months Fixed Term, Whole-time Post The postdoctoral researcher / senior postdoctoral researcher will modify an existing GIS-based multicriteria decision support tool in order to designate optimal areas for offshore windfarm development from Clew Bay to the north coast of the island of Ireland to the northern Irish Sea. Building on a model for NW Ireland, the researcher will collate all available spatial datasets of relevance to offshore windfarm development, standardise within a GIS, and consolidate into combined datasets through expert weighted or numerical modelling. Further weightings will be undertaken through a stakeholder-driven Analytic Hierarchical Process or similar. New MOSAIC-generated megafaunal distribution data will be showcased in the mode with its impact qualified. Liaison with government and stakeholder agencies in the Republic of Ireland and Northern Ireland (UK) will ensure policy relevant outputs. The candidate should be proficient in GIS and Python with, ideally, a familiarity with the offshore windfarm sector and marine geomatics. Please note that Garda vetting and/or an international police clearance check may form part of the selection process. Project : GSI-based multicriteria decision support tool development for north of Ireland offshore windfarm site suitability modelling For an information package including full details of the post, selection criteria and application process see https://ore.ucc.ie/ The University, at its discretion, may undertake to make an additional appointment(s) from this competition following the conclusion of the process. Informal inquiries can be made in confidence to Professor Andy Wheeler, Professor of Geology and Principle Investigator, School of Biological, Earth & Environmental Sciences, Tel: + 353 (0) 87 6621038; Email: a.wheeler@ucc.ie For further information on the hiring unit, please see: https://www.ucc.ie/en/bees/ University College Cork is committed to being a fully inclusive global university which actively recruits, supports and retains colleagues from all sectors of society. Equality, Diversity and Inclusion (EDI) are core values under our UCC Strategic Plan 2023-2028. UCC holds a Silver Athena SWAN award in recognition of our commitment to advancing equality in higher education. We value diversity as well as celebrate, support and thrive on the contributions of all our employees and the communities they represent. We are proud to be an equal opportunities employer and encourage applications from everybody, regardless of age, care-giving status, disability, ethnicity, gender and/or gender identity or expression status, nationality, marital status/civil partnership, pregnancy and maternity, race, religion/creed, and/or sexual orientation. We are committed to supporting all staff through flexible working schemes, family-friendly policies, training and development, and staff networks. We value the enrichment that comes from a diverse community and seek to promote equality, prevent discrimination and protect the human rights of each individual in line with equality legislation. We encourage applicants to consult our Dignity and Respect Policy and learn more about our EDI related initiatives Salary: Post-Doctoral Researcher: €47,273 - €53,925 p.a (IUA PD1 Salary Scale), Senior Post-Doctoral Researcher: €55,339 - 60250 p.a. (IUA PD2 Salary Scale) Salary placement on appointment will be in accordance with public sector pay policy. We encourage you to reach out to us directly should you require assistance or reasonable accommodation during the recruitment process. Please note interviews will be conducted either online via Microsoft Teams or in person in the first instance. Candidates may also be required to attend interviews in person if an interview takes place online. Candidates will be notified as appropriate Applications must be submitted online via the University College Cork vacancy portal (https://ore.ucc.ie/). Queries relating to the online application process should be referred to hrresearchqueries@ucc.ie quoting the job-title. Candidates should apply, in confidence, before 12 noon (Irish Local Time) on Friday, 23rd October 2026. No late applications will be accepted. UNIVERSITY COLLEGE CORK IS AN EQUAL OPPORTUNITIES EMPLOYER Please note that an appointment to posts advertised will be dependent on University approval, together with the terms of the employment control framework for the higher education sector. Contact Person : Prof. Andrew Wheeler Contact Email : a.wheeler@ucc.ie Job ID : 099473 Contact Number : +353 87 662 1038 Close Date : 23-Oct-2026 12:00 "
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/uccrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=099613": {
      "title": "Research Assistant (Technical) School of Biochemistry and Cell Biology",
      "description": "Closing Date: 23/10/2026 Research Assistant (Technical) School of Biochemistry and Cell Biology 18 Months Fixed-Term, Whole-Time Post Applications are invited for a Research Assistant position in the Cell Biology Laboratory, in the School of Biochemistry and Cell Biology to work on a Research Ireland- funded Frontiers for the Future Award research programme. The successful candidate will work within this research team to carry out research on cell signalling in the context of inflammatory disorders and aggressive cancers. Experimental approaches to be applied will include culture and transfection/infection of mammalian cell lines including CRISPR gene editing, protein structure function studies, advanced cell imaging, flow cytometry, western blotting/immunoprecipitation, and a range of cell and protein function assays. The successful candidate is expected to have at minimum at BSc or MSc or equivalent qualification, to be enthusiastic about scientific enquiry, and to have experience in some of the experimental approaches outlined above. They will join a supportive and stimulating environment that fosters excellent research, high quality publications, and excellent opportunities for career development. Please note that Garda vetting and/or an international police clearance check may form part of the selection process. Project : Exploiting the spatial actions of metabolic and survival factors for therapeutic benefit For an information package including full details of the post, selection criteria and application process see https://ore.ucc.ie/. The University, at its discretion, may undertake to make an additional appointment(s) from this competition following the conclusion of the process. Informal enquiries can be made in confidence to Dr. Rosemary O’Connor Tel: + 353 (0) 21 4901312 Email: r.oconnor@ucc.ie For further information on the hiring unit, please see: https://www.ucc.ie/en/biochemistry/ University College Cork is committed to being a fully inclusive global university which actively recruits, supports and retains colleagues from all sectors of society. Equality, Diversity and Inclusion (EDI) are core values under our UCC Strategic Plan 2023-2028. UCC holds a Silver Athena SWAN award in recognition of our commitment to advancing equality in higher education. We value diversity as well as celebrate, support and thrive on the contributions of all our employees and the communities they represent. We are proud to be an equal opportunities employer and encourage applications from everybody, regardless of age, care-giving status, disability, ethnicity, gender and/or gender identity or expression status, nationality, marital status/civil partnership, pregnancy and maternity, race, religion/creed, and/or sexual orientation. We are committed to supporting all staff through flexible working schemes, family-friendly policies, training and development, and staff networks. We value the enrichment that comes from a diverse community and seek to promote equality, prevent discrimination and protect the human rights of each individual in line with equality legislation. We encourage applicants to consult our Dignity and Respect Policy and learn more about our EDI related initiatives Salary: €34,129 - €44,311 p.a (IUA RA Salary Scale) Salary placement on appointment will be in accordance with public sector pay policy. We encourage you to reach out to us directly should you require assistance or reasonable accommodation during the recruitment process. Please note interviews will be conducted either online via Microsoft Teams or in person in the first instance. Candidates may also be required to attend interviews in person if an interview takes place online. Candidates will be notified as appropriate Applications must be submitted online via the University College Cork vacancy portal (https://ore.ucc.ie/). Queries relating to the online application process should be referred to hrresearchqueries@ucc.ie quoting the job-title. Candidates should apply, in confidence, before 12 noon (Irish Local Time) on Friday, 23rd October 2026. No late applications will be accepted. UNIVERSITY COLLEGE CORK IS AN EQUAL OPPORTUNITIES EMPLOYER Please note that an appointment to posts advertised will be dependent on University approval, together with the terms of the employment control framework for the higher education sector. Contact Person : Dr. Rosemary O’Connor Contact Email : r.oconnor@ucc.ie Job ID : 099613 Contact Number : Close Date : 23-Oct-2026 12:00 "
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/uccrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=098373": {
      "title": "School Manager, School of History",
      "description": "Closing Date: 03/11/2026 School Manager, School of History COLLEGE OF ARTS, CELTIC STUDIES & SOCIAL SCIENCES Permanent Whole-Time Post UCC wishes to appoint an administrator to the role of School Manager. Reporting to the Head of School, the School Manager will be responsible, with the Head of School, for co-ordinating and supervising the operation of all administrative and support functions in the School of History. In order to do so, they will oversee the management the School’s finances in accordance with the policies and procedures set down by the University and play a key role in implementing the strategic plans of the School of History. Please note that Garda vetting and/or an international police clearance check may form part of the selection process. For an information package including full details of the post, selection criteria and application process see https://ore.ucc.ie/. The University, at its discretion, may undertake to make an additional appointment(s) from this competition following the conclusion of the process. Informal enquiries can be made in confidence to Dr Damian Bracken, email: d.bracken@ucc.ie For further information on the Department https://www.ucc.ie/en/history/ University College Cork is committed to being a fully inclusive global university which actively recruits, supports and retains colleagues from all sectors of society. Equality, Diversity and Inclusion (EDI) are core values under our UCC Strategic Plan 2023-2028. UCC holds a Silver Athena SWAN award in recognition of our commitment to advancing equality in higher education. We value diversity as well as celebrate, support and thrive on the contributions of all our employees and the communities they represent. We are proud to be an equal opportunities employer and encourage applications from everybody, regardless of age, care-giving status, disability, ethnicity, gender and/or gender identity or expression status, nationality, marital status/civil partners